        "research_rationale": "EO 12121 (signed 1979-02-26, 44 FR 11195) read in full, with EO 12083 (parent), EO 12156 and EO 12379 read in the relevant parts from the held official FR texts. Identity confirmed. The order is a one-sentence amendment of Sec. 1-102 of EO 12083 (adds two ex officio members). First and whole-order end: EO 12379 Sec. 20 revoking EO 12083 'as amended' (1982-08-17, on signing), with the reason that the amendment has no operation once its parent is revoked; EO 12121 is not named by number, which is stated in the clause reason with the alternative reading. The dossier's ACT lead for this pair cites only the APP mirror of EO 12379; I used the held FR text of EO 12379. Later event: the EO 12156 further amendment. Savings: none_after_bounded_search. AI producer hypothesis only; not human certification.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"No instrument other than EO 12379 is shown to have ended this order or its parent before 1982-08-17: the Cruden scan of EO 12083 and EO 12121 found only EO 12148, EO 12156 and EO 12379 citing them (EO 12148 and EO 12156 add a further member, FEMA; the sequence is later event material, not an end); the dossier chain lists EO 12156 (amendment) and EO 12379 (revocation as amended); current-law:usc and current-law:ecfr recorded no hit.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"No independent command: the addition operates only inside EO 12083 Sec. 1-102 and has no standing apart from it.\",\"savings_check\":\"No savings or residual effect is shown: EO 12379 has no savings wording; the revoked Committee's membership list has no function after revocation, and no held text transfers the Committee's functions.\",\"scope_check\":\"The order has one operative sentence (adding members (x) and (y) to Sec. 1-102 of EO 12083), so the single whole-order clause ends on one date.\"}",
